  "appliesTo": "Most schools in the Wakefield District have the same term and holiday dates. These dates are set and agreed by the Council.",
  "academyNote": "Voluntary-aided schools and academies can set their own term and holiday dates. If your child attends one of these types of school, you should contact the school directly to check their dates.",
  "localFacts": [
    {
      "fact": "Most schools in the Wakefield District share the same term and holiday dates, which are set and agreed by the council.",
      "source": "https://www.wakefield.gov.uk/schools-and-education/schools/school-term-and-holiday-dates"
    },
    {
      "fact": "Each school sets five INSET days a year, agreed by its governing body.",
      "source": "https://www.wakefield.gov.uk/schools-and-education/schools/school-term-and-holiday-dates"
    },
    {
      "fact": "A school used as a polling station on district council election day must get the Returning Officer's permission to stay open, otherwise it closes for an INSET day.",
      "source": "https://www.wakefield.gov.uk/schools-and-education/schools/202627-school-calendar"
    },
    {
      "fact": "A draft 2028-29 calendar is published but not yet approved; the council will decide on it in spring 2027.",
      "source": "https://www.wakefield.gov.uk/schools-and-education/schools/school-term-and-holiday-dates"
    },
    {
      "fact": "In 2026-27 the Easter holiday starts on Good Friday, 26 March 2027, and schools go back on Monday 12 April 2027.",
      "source": "https://www.wakefield.gov.uk/schools-and-education/schools/202627-school-calendar"
    },
    {
      "fact": "In 2027-28 the summer holiday starts on Wednesday 26 July 2028, and a PDF of that calendar is available on request from the school place planning team.",
